#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:263
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "For each string nobody has adjudicated, its candidates are ranked: official 0, adjudicated 1, a person's proposal 2, a translation platform (Weblate, Crowdin, Transifex) 3, an agent model 4, machine translation 5; a QA failure adds 10; ties go to the newest; a stale candidate, made for another source text, is never picked. An empty `msgstr`, or one that is itself an earlier auto-pick, takes the best: fuzzy and unofficial (`chosen.how: auto`), except an official candidate whose English matches the msgid exactly, which is written as `auto-official`. A collaborator's choice, and text whose provenance is not an auto-pick, are never overwritten. `translation-strings.ts` `applyAutoPick`; the 🌐 pane ranks with the same function's rules."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:166
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "For each wrong string: pick a ranked candidate, which fills an editable box (its source is recorded with the suggestion while its text is unedited), or type your own. Anyone's text is a proposal. An owner, member or collaborator may also tick Choose as the translation and say why: the suggestion then carries `choose: true` and the `reason`, and it is recorded as the string's translation only once the workflow has confirmed who they are. The suggestion carries the text the reviewer saw (`current`), so a choice against a catalogue that changed under them is caught."
msgstr ""

