#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "On every page, source-language pages included, a block's 📣 panel has a 🌐 pane that lists every locale's current translation of the block, its status, and how it came to be (`chosen.how`, `chosen.by`). On a translated page its own locale comes first and the others are collapsed. ✎ Fix translation opens, per locale, each of the block's strings with its candidates ranked as the auto-pick ranks them: the text; the source's kind, id and version; who proposed it, linked to the issue it came from; the date; its QA results; a stale mark when it was made for another source text; whether an official source's English matched exactly; and which one is the default."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One or more candidate sources write alternatives per string to `translations/<locale>/<catalogue>.candidates.json` (`translation-candidates/v1`), each candidate carrying its source: an agent model, an open machine-translation model, a web service, or a person. The engines are interchangeable behind one skill, `translation-candidate-source`: whichever runs, the same sidecar comes out. Writers append; a candidate is never a verdict."
msgstr ""

