#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:175
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Submit opens GitHub's new-issue form prefilled with a readable summary and a `translation-adjudication/v1` JSON block, labelled `translation-adjudication` and titled `[translation review] …`. The summary says, per string, whether the author proposes or chooses. When the record is too long for a URL the page copies the body for pasting instead. Filing it is the act of proposing, or, for a collaborator who chose, of adjudicating."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:325
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The chosen text is the string's translation, not fuzzy; the pane shows it `adjudicated`, by whom and why, until the source text changes and it shows `stale`. Like a reviewed catalogue, it is still not official."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:292
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The maintainer checks that the PR writes down what the issue decided and nothing else, lets the layer's checks run, and merges or closes it."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only lane that judges a translation. The person who files the issue is the reviewer: their GitHub login is the only identity the record carries, and nothing they type in the body can name anyone else. Whoever they are, what they file is recorded as a proposal; it is an adjudication only when the workflow finds them an owner, member or collaborator (`author_association`) and they asked to choose. Choosing a candidate is a judgement too, so the candidate's source is recorded with it."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:234
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The pins bind adjudication only. Per verdict and per choice: is the catalogue's hash today the one the page showed, does its path stay inside the translations directory, and is the suggestion's `current` text still what the catalogue says? One that fails is refused with its reason (reload the page and choose again), and its proposal is kept. `No` when no choice or acceptance survives: the proposals still go on to the auto-pick. `Yes` when at least one survives, and the refusals are reported beside what was recorded."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:330
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The proposals are in the sidecar, beside every other candidate; a string with no translation of its own shows the best-ranked one, fuzzy, so the catalogue still needs review: a person's text is not reviewed by being written. A collaborator choosing among them is a new instance of this process."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:320
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The review page shows the catalogue `reviewed`, and `stale` once its bytes change. It is still not official: locale sign-off is `human-translation-workflow`'s `Task_Signoff`, a separate act by the translation coordinator."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer opens the review page and reads one catalogue's strings against their source, with the candidates beside each."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:187
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The workflow runs for an issue that is labelled or titled as an adjudication, and once per issue: `Yes` when the issue's branch already exists, and nothing more is done."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:16
#. Diagram label
msgid "Translation review and adjudication"
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two fixed programs and no judgement: the candidate engines and the page generator before the review, the adjudication workflow after it. Every refusal on the right of this lane is the workflow declining to guess, and each says why on the issue. It never merges and never signs a locale off."
msgstr ""

#: library/processes/translation-review-adjudication.bpmn:127
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two ways in, one record out. `Review page`: a reader working through a layer's catalogues. `A block's 🌐`: a reader on any page who finds one block's translation wrong, or wants to see it. Both file the same `translation-adjudication/v1` issue."
msgstr ""

